{"time":"2026-07-22T21:19:50.526Z","line":"add","sessionID":"ses_07457bc60ffep1hRG1aNzrHY1g","job":"default","label":"default: every idle -> # CFMesh-AutoGUI — NIVEAU COMMERCIALE LOOP # Istruzioni: esegui QUESTO blocco a ogni iterazione. # Ogni iterazione implementa UNA feature da P0. # DOPO ogni iterazione → `python -m py_compile` + `pytest tests/ -x`. # Se fallisce: correggi e ripeti (max 3 cicli). # Quando tutte le P0 sono verdi → passa alle P1. # Quando tutte le P1 sono verdi → report finale. from octopoda import OctopodaRuntime octo = OctopodaRuntime() octo.remember(\"phase\", \"commercial_loop_v3\") octo.log_event(\"agent\", \"loop_start\", {\"version\": \"3.0.0\"}) # ============================================================= # ARCHITETTURA GENERALE — non modificare, segui ciecamente # ============================================================= # app/ → Entry point (già OK) # src/cfmesh_autogui/ # core/ → Logica mesh, geometria, CFD # gui/ → UI, viewer, pannelli # commercial/ → [NUOVO] Funzionalità commercial-level # plugins/ → SISTEMA A PLUGIN (già OK, da popolare) # tests/ → 1 test per ogni modulo, coverage > 85% # templates/ → Template casi (già OK) # locale/ → i18n IT/EN/DE/FR/ES/ZH/JA (da espandere) # installer/ → NSIS + Inno Setup (da migliorare) # cloud/ → [NUOVO] Integrazione cloud # ============================================================= # PRINCIPI FONDAMENTALI (vincoli assoluti) # ============================================================= # 1. OGNI funzione DEVE avere type hints completi # 2. OGNI modulo DEVE avere docstring PEP 257 # 3. OGNI funzione DEVE essere testabile (pytest, fixture) # 4. OGNI modifica DEVE passare `ruff check --fix` # 5. OGNI nuova dipendenza DEVE essere giustificata in pyproject.toml # 6. ZERO hardcoded path — usa QStandardPaths o AppSettings # 7. ZERO QTimer.sleep/sync wait — usa QThread + segnali # 8. UX: ANSYS Workbench-inspired, ribbon, workflow tree # 9. Tutti gli errori DEI finestra di dialogo modale + log # 10. NIENTE print() — usa logging.getLogger(__name__) # ============================================================= # P0 — CORE COMMERCIALE (da implementare SUBITO) # ============================================================= # Se una P0 è già implementata, skippala e vai alla prossima. # --- P0.1: WATER-TIGHT WORKFLOW AUTOMATICO --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/watertight.py # Ispirato a: Fluent Meshing Watertight Workflow # Cosa fa: # 1. Import geometry (STEP/STL/brep/IGES) # 2. Detect leaks & non-watertight edges → heal automatico # 3. Feature extraction: sharp edges, curvature, thin gaps # 4. Auto-size: based on local curvature + thickness (già in geometry.py) # 5. Add local refinement: box/cylinder/sphere/point sources # 6. Boundary layer: auto-detect walls, layers N/ratio/h # 7. Generate volume mesh: Cartesian + polyhedral + prism layer # 8. Check quality: checkMesh → report → auto-fix loop # 9. Export in tutti i formati # UI: Nuovo wizard \"Watertight Workflow\" a 5 passi con preview 3D live # Test: tests/test_watertight_workflow.py — full E2E # --- P0.2: FAULT-TOLERANT MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/fault_tolerant.py # Ispirato a: Fluent Meshing Fault-Tolerant Workflow # Cosa fa: # 1. Importa geometria anche NON watertight (STL con gap, overlapping) # 2. Wrap geometry: shrink-wrap surface mesh su geometria sporca # 3. Occlude internal features: riempie cavità interne non desiderate # 4. Local refinement + BL su wrap # 5. Volume fill con polyhedral/cartesian # 6. Quality check # UI: Checkbox \"Fault-Tolerant Mode\" nel wizard + param: gap_h, occlude_features # Test: tests/test_fault_tolerant.py — geometry with 0.1mm gap # --- P0.3: MOSAIC / POLY-HEDRAL CONNECTIVITY --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/mosaic.py # Ispirato a: Star-CCM+ Mosaic Technology # Cosa fa: # 1. Generate hex-dominant core (cfMesh cartesianMesh) # 2. Detect interface polyhedral → hex transition layer # 3. Generate conformal polyhedral cap layer # 4. Generate prism layer near walls (optional, già esiste) # 5. Quality optimization: smooth interface gradiente # Key: Rapporto di volume < 1:10 alla transizione hex→poly # Test: tests/test_mosaic.py # --- P0.4: BLOCK-STRUCTURED / O-GRID MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/block_mesh.py # Ispirato a: Pointwise, Cubit # Cosa fa: # 1. Decomposizione geometrica in blocchi (block topology) # 2. Edge associativo: associa spigoli blocco a curve CAD # 3. Mesh 2D strutturata su facce (transfinite interpolation) # 4. O-grid intorno a geometrie interne (butterfly grid) # 5. Extrude 2D→3D per sweepable geometry # 6. Merge blocchi → mesh multi-blocco strutturata # UI: Block editor grafico nel viewer (draw edges, assign patches) # Test: tests/test_block_mesh.py # --- P0.5: ADAPTIVE MESH REFINEMENT (AMR) --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/amr.py # Ispirato a: OpenFOAM dynamicRefineFvMesh, Star-CCM+ AMR # Cosa fa: # 1. Solution-based refinement: legge field (U, p, nut) da OpenFOAM # 2. Gradient-based: refine dove |∇φ| > threshold # 3. Curvature-based: refine su feature geometriche # 4. Error estimation: Hessian-based o adjoint-based # 5. Coarsening: de-refine dove gradiente basso # 6. Hanging node constraints: hanging node handling 2:1 rule # 7. Interpolation: solution mapping tra mesh successive # 8. Loop: refine → solve → check error → refine/coarsen (max 10 iter) # UI: AMR tab nel pannello Advanced con grafico convergenza live # Test: tests/test_amr.py # --- P0.6: OVERSET / CHIMERA GRIDS --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/overset.py # Ispirato a: suggar, Star-CCM+ Overset # Cosa fa: # 1. Background mesh (fondo statico) # 2. Overset component mesh (body-attached, si muove) # 3. Hole cutting: foro nel background dove overlap # 4. Receptor identification: interpolation zone # 5. Donor search: nearest-neighbor / stencil # 6. Fringe assembly: connect background + overset # 7. Quality: check overlap ratio, orphan cells # UI: \"Overset Region\" dock + motion definition (translating/rotating/6DOF) # Test: tests/test_overset.py # --- P0.7: BOUNDARY LAYER QUALITY ENGINE --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/bl_engine.py # Ispirato a: ANSA Boundary Layer, Pointwise T-Rex # Cosa fa: # 1. Automatic wall detection (angle-based + patch naming) # 2. BL parameters: first_layer_height, n_layers, growth_rate # 3. y+ estimation: calcola y+ atteso per Re, U_ref, turbolenza # 4. Conformal BL su geometria complessa (corners, convex/concave) # 5. BL collision detection: dove BL si sovrappone → merge / reduce # 6. BL smoothing: node redistribution per qualità ortogonale # 7. BL quality metrics: skewness, non-orthogonality, aspect ratio # 8. BL on patches selezionati (non obbligatorio su tutti i wall) # 9. Visualization: BL thickness isosurface, y+ contour # UI: BL Expert Mode con tabella layers, grafico y+ estimato, visual preview # Test: tests/test_bl_engine.py # --- P0.8: MESH QUALITY OPTIMIZATION ENGINE --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/optimizer.py # Ispirato a: MeshLab, Star-CCM+ Optimizer, Ansys Meshing # Cosa fa: # 1. Quality metrics: aspect ratio, skewness, non-orthogonality, # determinant, jacobian, cell volume, face validity, twist # 2. Smoothing: Laplace + Taubin + constrained optimization # 3. Topological improvement: edge flips, face swapping # 4. Node relocation: optimization-based (minimize max skewness) # 5. Pillow: hex quality improvement via sheet extraction # 6. Quality-aware refinement: refine bad cells only # 7. Report: before/after metrics, histogram, spatial quality map # 8. Loop: fix → eval → fix (max 5 iter, stop se converged) # UI: Quality tab con heatmap 3D, histogram, auto-fix button, report PDF # Test: tests/test_optimizer.py # --- P0.9: CAD DEFEATURING & HEALING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/cad_healer.py # Ispirato a: ANSA CAD Cleanup, SpaceClaim # Cosa fa: # 1. Detect small features: holes < threshold, fillets, chamfers, ribs # 2. Automatic defeaturing: fill holes, remove blends, suppress features # 3. Imprint/merge: merge lines of adjacent faces # 4. Stitch: close gaps between adjacent faces # 5. Remove sliver faces: merge narrow faces (< min_area) # 6. Watertight check: isClosed manifold test # 7. Simplify: reduce facet count (STL decimation) preservando feature # 8. Re-topology: quad-dominant retopology per mesh strutturata # UI: Defeature tab con parametri: hole_diam, fillet_radius, sliver_area # Test: tests/test_cad_healer.py # --- P0.10: PARALLEL MESHING ENGINE --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/parallel_mesh.py # Ispirato a: cfMesh parallel, OpenFOAM decomposePar # Cosa fa: # 1. Geometry decomposition (metis/scotch) # 2. Parallel surface meshing (domain decomposition) # 3. Parallel volume meshing (subdomain mesh, overlap) # 4. Mesh stitching: stitch subdomain interfaces # 5. Load balancing: dynamic repartitioning # 6. MPI integration: mpiexec -np N cartesianMesh # 7. Progress bar: per-subdomain + global # 8. Result: merged parallel mesh → single polyMesh # UI: Advanced tab → Parallel Meshing → N cores selector (da 2 a 128) # Test: tests/test_parallel_mesh.py # ============================================================= # P1 — FEATURES PROFESSIONALI (dopo tutte le P0) # ============================================================= # --- P1.1: MULTI-REGION CONFORMAL INTERFACES --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/multi_region.py # Per CHT, FSI, conjugate heat transfer # Crea regioni con interfacce conformali (node-match) # --- P1.2: MESH MORPHING / DEFORMATION --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/morphing.py # Ispirato a: ANSA Morphing, DepMorpher # B-spline/FFD-based mesh deformation per optimization # --- P1.3: TEMPLATE-BASED BATCH MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/batch_mesh.py # Journal system: registra azioni → replay su N geometrie # Queue: batch processing su coda di file # CLI: headless mode per CI/CD # --- P1.4: MESH CONVERSION & EXPORT FACTORY --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/exporter.py # Output: OpenFOAM, CGNS, VTU/VTM, Ansys .cas/.h5, Abaqus .inp, # Star-CCM+ .ccm, SU2, Fluent .msh, GMSH .msh, TetGen .poly # --- P1.5: AI/ML-ASSISTED MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/ai_mesh.py # ML model predice: # - Optimal cell size field (data-driven sizing) # - Mesh quality prediction (prima di generare) # - Auto-BL parameters (y+, layers, growth) # - Solver-specific mesh recommendations (LES vs RANS) # --- P1.6: REAL-TIME QUALITY DASHBOARD --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/monitor.py # 3D heatmap di qualità aggiornata in tempo reale # Metrics: skewness, non-orthogonality, aspect ratio # Identifica e mostra le N celle peggiori con coordinate # --- P1.7: COLLABORATIVE / CLOUD MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/cloud_mesh.py # Invia job a cluster Slurm / AWS Batch / Azure Batch # Session sharing: condividi caso via link (collaborazione) # GitHub/GitLab integration: version control per progetti mesh # --- P1.8: JOURNAL / MACRO RECORDER --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/journal.py # Ogni azione utente → registrata in journal.json # Playback: replay con diverso geometry file # Scripting: Python API per automazione # --- P1.9: IMMERSIVE MESH INSPECTION (AR/VR) --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/xr_viewer.py # Esporta mesh per Unity/Unreal # WebXR-based VR inspector da browser # VR section cut, VR quality painting # --- P1.10: TOPOLOGY OPTIMIZATION-AWARE MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/topo_mesh.py # Lattice/infill mesh generation # Density-based mesh adaptation # STL-to-lattice conversion # ============================================================= # P2 — ENTERPRISE / ECOSISTEMA (quando P0+P1 sono verdi) # ============================================================= # P2.1: Licensing — FlexNet-style floating license o subscription # P2.2: Audit trail — blockchain-backed (già Octopoda, da estendere) # P2.3: SSO/SAML — Azure AD, Okta, Google Workspace # P2.4: API REST — FastAPI per headless + CI/CD integration # P2.5: Dashboard analitica — Grafana + InfluxDB, metriche d'uso # P2.6: Plugin Marketplace — download/install plugin da repository # P2.7: Enterprise installer — MSI con GPO deploy, silent install # P2.8: Documentation engine — Sphinx auto-generata da docstring # ============================================================= # TESTS — regole obbligatorie # ============================================================= # DOPO ogni implementazione: # 1. `python -m py_compile src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/NOME_MODULO.py` # 2. `pytest tests/test_NOME_MODULO.py -x --tb=short -q` # 3. Se fallisce → analizza stderr → correggi → rigenera test → ripeti (max 3) # 4. `ruff check --fix src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/NOME_MODULO.py` # 5. Se tutto OK → octo.log_event(\"agent\", f\"P0.{N}_done\", {\"module\": \"NOME_MODULO\"}) # ============================================================= # UX — ANSYS WORKBENCH INSPIRED (vincoli assoluti) # ============================================================= # - Ribbon toolbar: Home | Geometry | Mesh | Advanced | Quality | Export # - Workflow tree: progressivo con icone (✅/⏳/❌/⬜) # - Ogni modale DEVE essere non-bloccante (show, non exec) # - Preview 3D live: ogni cambiamento parametro → update viewer # - Tooltip su OGNI parametro con formula/significato fisico # - Shortcuts: Ctrl+N (new), Ctrl+O (open), Ctrl+R (reload), # Ctrl+M (mesh it!), Ctrl+Shift+Q (quick quality check) # - Status bar: mesh count, quality summary, WSL status, license # ============================================================= # PERFORMANCE # ============================================================= # - Mesh > 10M celle → progress bar + ETA + memory usage # - Lazy loading: geometry preview a bassa risoluzione # - Worker thread per OGNI operazione lunga (>0.5s) # - Cache: risultati curvature/thickness caching su disco # - Memory: release mesh dal viewer dopo N minuti di inattività # ============================================================= # REPORT & EXPORT # ============================================================= # Ogni esecuzione produce: # 1. PDF quality report (reportlab) con: metriche, histogram, screenshot # 2. JSON report per integrazione CI/CD # 3. Octopoda audit log per debug e riproducibilità # 4. Mesh file in formato selezionato # 5. OpenFOAM case completo (controlDict, fvSchemes, fvSolution, fields) # ============================================================= # CHIAMATA RICORSIVA — loop pattern # ============================================================= # Al termine di OGNI iterazione: # legacy = octo.recall(\"implemented_features\") or [] # legacy.append({ # \"feature\": feature_name, # \"module\": module_path, # \"tests\": test_file, # \"status\": \"PASS\" if all_tests_pass else \"FAIL\" # }) # octo.remember(\"implemented_features\", legacy) # # if len(legacy) < TOTAL_FEATURES: # octo.log_event(\"agent\", \"loop_continue\", {\"implemented\": len(legacy)}) # # TORNA ALL'INIZIO di questo prompt e scegli la prossima P0 non implementata # else: # octo.log_event(\"agent\", \"loop_complete\", {\"total\": len(legacy)}) # octo.log_event(\"agent\", \"final_report\", legacy) # print(f\"✅ COMMERCIAL LEVEL COMPLETE — {len(legacy)} features implemented\")"}
