n\" dock + motion definition (translating/rotating/6DOF) # Test: tests/test_overset.py # --- P0.7: BOUNDARY LAYER QUALITY ENGINE --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/bl_engine.py # Ispirato a: ANSA Boundary Layer, Pointwise T-Rex # Cosa fa: # 1. Automatic wall detection (angle-based + patch naming) # 2. BL parameters: first_layer_height, n_layers, growth_rate # 3. y+ estimation: calcola y+ atteso per Re, U_ref, turbolenza # 4. Conformal BL su geometria complessa (corners, convex/concave) # 5. BL collision detection: dove BL si sovrappone → merge / reduce # 6. BL smoothing: node redistribution per qualità ortogonale # 7. BL quality metrics: skewness, non-orthogonality, aspect ratio # 8. BL on patches selezionati (non obbligatorio su tutti i wall) # 9. Visualization: BL thickness isosurface, y+ contour # UI: BL Expert Mode con tabella layers, grafico y+ estimato, visual preview # Test: tests/test_bl_engine.py # --- P0.8: MESH QUALITY OPTIMIZATION ENGINE --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/optimizer.py # Ispirato a: MeshLab, Star-CCM+ Optimizer, Ansys Meshing # Cosa fa: # 1. Quality metrics: aspect ratio, skewness, non-orthogonality, # determinant, jacobian, cell volume, face validity, twist # 2. Smoothing: Laplace + Taubin + constrained optimization # 3. Topological improvement: edge flips, face swapping # 4. Node relocation: optimization-based (minimize max skewness) # 5. Pillow: hex quality improvement via sheet extraction # 6. Quality-aware refinement: refine bad cells only # 7. Report: before/after metrics, histogram, spatial quality map # 8. Loop: fix → eval → fix (max 5 iter, stop se converged) # UI: Quality tab con heatmap 3D, histogram, auto-fix button, report PDF # Test: tests/test_optimizer.py # --- P0.9: CAD DEFEATURING & HEALING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/cad_healer.py # Ispirato a: ANSA CAD Cleanup, SpaceClaim # Cosa fa: # 1. Detect small features: holes < threshold, fillets, chamfers, ribs # 2. Automatic defeaturing: fill holes, remove blends, suppress features # 3. Imprint/merge: merge lines of adjacent faces # 4. Stitch: close gaps between adjacent faces # 5. Remove sliver faces: merge narrow faces (< min_area) # 6. Watertight check: isClosed manifold test # 7. Simplify: reduce facet count (STL decimation) preservando feature # 8. Re-topology: quad-dominant retopology per mesh strutturata # UI: Defeature tab con parametri: hole_diam, fillet_radius, sliver_area # Test: tests/test_cad_healer.py # --- P0.10: PARALLEL MESHING ENGINE --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/parallel_mesh.py # Ispirato a: cfMesh parallel, OpenFOAM decomposePar # Cosa fa: # 1. Geometry decomposition (metis/scotch) # 2. Parallel surface meshing (domain decomposition) # 3. Parallel volume meshing (subdomain mesh, overlap) # 4. Mesh stitching: stitch subdomain interfaces # 5. Load balancing: dynamic repartitioning # 6. MPI integration: mpiexec -np N cartesianMesh # 7. Progress bar: per-subdomain + global # 8. Result: merged parallel mesh → single polyMesh # UI: Advanced tab → Parallel Meshing → N cores selector (da 2 a 128) # Test: tests/test_parallel_mesh.py # ============================================================= # P1 — FEATURES PROFESSIONALI (dopo tutte le P0) # ============================================================= # --- P1.1: MULTI-REGION CONFORMAL INTERFACES --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/multi_region.py # Per CHT, FSI, conjugate heat transfer # Crea regioni con interfacce conformali (node-match) # --- P1.2: MESH MORPHING / DEFORMATION --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/morphing.py # Ispirato a: ANSA Morphing, DepMorpher # B-spline/FFD-based mesh deformation per optimization # --- P1.3: TEMPLATE-BASED BATCH MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/batch_mesh.py # Journal system: registra azioni → replay su N geometrie # Queue: batch processing su coda di file # CLI: headless mode per CI/CD # --- P1.4: MESH CONVERSION & EXPORT FACTORY --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/exporter.py # Output: OpenFOAM, CGNS, VTU/VTM, Ansys .cas/.h5, Abaqus .inp, # Star-CCM+ .ccm, SU2, Fluent .msh, GMSH .msh, TetGen .poly # --- P1.5: AI/ML-ASSISTED MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/ai_mesh.py # ML model predice: # - Optimal cell size field (data-driven sizing) # - Mesh quality prediction (prima di generare) # - Auto-BL parameters (y+, layers, growth) # - Solver-specific mesh recommendations (LES vs RANS) # --- P1.6: REAL-TIME QUALITY DASHBOARD --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/monitor.py # 3D heatmap di qualità aggiornata in tempo reale # Metrics: skewness, non-orthogonality, aspect ratio # Identifica e mostra le N celle peggiori con coordinate # --- P1.7: COLLABORATIVE / CLOUD MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/cloud_mesh.py # Invia job a cluster Slurm / AWS Batch / Azure Batch # Session sharing: condividi caso via link (collaborazione) # GitHub/GitLab integration: version control per progetti mesh # --- P1.8: JOURNAL / MACRO RECORDER --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/journal.py # Ogni azione utente → registrata in journal.json # Playback: replay con diverso geometry file # Scripting: Python API per automazione # --- P1.9: IMMERSIVE MESH INSPECTION (AR/VR) --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/xr_viewer.py # Esporta mesh per Unity/Unreal # WebXR-based VR inspector da browser # VR section cut, VR quality painting # --- P1.10: TOPOLOGY OPTIMIZATION-AWARE MESHING --- # Modulo: src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/topo_mesh.py # Lattice/infill mesh generation # Density-based mesh adaptation # STL-to-lattice conversion # ============================================================= # P2 — ENTERPRISE / ECOSISTEMA (quando P0+P1 sono verdi) # ============================================================= # P2.1: Licensing — FlexNet-style floating license o subscription # P2.2: Audit trail — blockchain-backed (già Octopoda, da estendere) # P2.3: SSO/SAML — Azure AD, Okta, Google Workspace # P2.4: API REST — FastAPI per headless + CI/CD integration # P2.5: Dashboard analitica — Grafana + InfluxDB, metriche d'uso # P2.6: Plugin Marketplace — download/install plugin da repository # P2.7: Enterprise installer — MSI con GPO deploy, silent install # P2.8: Documentation engine — Sphinx auto-generata da docstring # ============================================================= # TESTS — regole obbligatorie # ============================================================= # DOPO ogni implementazione: # 1. `python -m py_compile src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/NOME_MODULO.py` # 2. `pytest tests/test_NOME_MODULO.py -x --tb=short -q` # 3. Se fallisce → analizza stderr → correggi → rigenera test → ripeti (max 3) # 4. `ruff check --fix src/cfmesh_autogui/commercial/NOME_MODULO.py` # 5. Se tutto OK → octo.log_event(\"agent\", f\"P0.{N}_done\", {\"module\": \"NOME_MODULO\"}) # ============================================================= # UX — ANSYS WORKBENCH INSPIRED (vincoli assoluti) # ============================================================= # - Ribbon toolbar: Home | Geometry | Mesh | Advanced | Quality | Export # - Workflow tree: progressivo con icone (✅/⏳/❌/⬜) # - Ogni modale DEVE essere non-bloccante (show, non exec) # - Preview 3D live: ogni cambiamento parametro → update viewer # - Tooltip su OGNI parametro con formula/significato fisico # - Shortcuts: Ctrl+N (new), Ctrl+O (open), Ctrl+R (reload), # Ctrl+M (mesh it!), Ctrl+Shift+Q (quick quality check) # - Status bar: mesh count, quality summary, WSL status, license # ============================================================= # PERFORMANCE # ============================================================= # - Mesh > 10M celle → progress bar + ETA + memory usage # - Lazy loading: geometry preview a bassa risoluzione # - Worker thread per OGNI operazione lunga (>0.5s) # - Cache: risultati curvature/thickness caching su disco # - Memory: release mesh dal viewer dopo N minuti di inattività # ============================================================= # REPORT & EXPORT # ============================================================= # Ogni esecuzione produce: # 1. PDF quality report (reportlab) con: metriche, histogram, screenshot # 2. JSON report per integrazione CI/CD # 3. Octopoda audit log per debug e riproducibilità # 4. Mesh file in formato selezionato # 5. OpenFOAM case completo (controlDict, fvSchemes, fvSolution, fields) # ============================================================= # CHIAMATA RICORSIVA — loop pattern # ============================================================= # Al termine di OGNI iterazione: # legacy = octo.recall(\"implemented_features\") or [] # legacy.append({ # \"feature\": feature_name, # \"module\": module_path, # \"tests\": test_file, # \"status\": \"PASS\" if all_tests_pass else \"FAIL\" # }) # octo.remember(\"implemented_features\", legacy) # # if len(legacy) < TOTAL_FEATURES: # octo.log_event(\"agent\", \"loop_continue\", {\"implemented\": len(legacy)}) # # TORNA ALL'INIZIO di questo prompt e scegli la prossima P0 non implementata # else: # octo.log_event(\"agent\", \"loop_complete\", {\"total\": len(legacy)}) # octo.log_event(\"agent\", \"final_report\", legacy) # print(f\"✅ COMMERCIAL LEVEL COMPLETE — {len(legacy)} features implemented\")"}
